sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Admin SPA (support)
    participant API as POST /api/v1/admin/merchants/{id}/deposit-credits
    participant Merchants as merchants service (credit_deposit)
    participant Ledger as wallet.service.post()
    participant Close as fulfillment.end_a_refunded_merchant_order
    participant DB as Postgres

    Admin->>API: amount, note, order_id? + Idempotency-Key: {client_key}
    Note over Admin: two SPA surfaces since M3c Task 4: the merchant page's general form<br/>(any amount, any order) and the ORDER page's one-button card, which fills<br/>the charge and the order id. The card is hidden unless the order is unsettled<br/>AND its delivery has terminally stopped (failure_reason in fulfillment_failed,<br/>order_failed) -- settling a live order is refused by the API below anyway
    API->>API: require header (422 without) -- it is the replay handle
    API->>Merchants: credit_deposit(key="merchant-credit:{merchant_id}:{client_key}", actor="admin:{id}", order_id?)
    Merchants->>DB: SELECT merchants WHERE id (404 if missing, frozen is fine -- freeze never blocks money in)
    opt order_id given -- settling one failed order
        Merchants->>DB: SELECT orders WHERE id = uuid(order_id) AND merchant_id
        Note over Merchants,DB: not this merchant's, no such order, not a UUID at all:<br/>ONE 404 order_not_found, so the refusal is no oracle
        Merchants->>DB: SELECT fulfillment_tasks WHERE order_id FOR UPDATE, then orders FOR UPDATE
        Note over Merchants,DB: tasks BEFORE the order -- the system-wide lock order. The drain claims<br/>with SKIP LOCKED, so it skips this order rather than blocking, which is<br/>what makes the next refusal total instead of a check-then-act
        alt any task pending or in_progress
            Merchants-->>Admin: 409 order_still_fulfilling {open_task_ids} -- cancel it first
            Note over Merchants: the terminal status a settlement writes is only true if the<br/>delivery is over, and retry/force-complete are guarded but the QUEUE<br/>is not. Skipped on a replay, like the over-settlement cap
        end
    end
    Merchants->>Ledger: ensure_account(merchant_deposit) + ensure_account(house_payments_received)
    Merchants->>Ledger: post(kind=merchant_deposit_credit, D merchant_deposit / C house_payments_received)
    Note over Merchants,Ledger: reference = order:{order_id} when given, else merchant:{merchant_id}.<br/>The legs never change -- only what the transaction is ABOUT
    Ledger->>DB: SELECT wallet_transactions WHERE idempotency_key
    alt key unseen -- first attempt
        Ledger->>DB: INSERT wallet_transactions + 2 wallet_postings (all-or-nothing)
        DB-->>Ledger: new transaction
    else key already owned -- admin retry (or amended amount/order_id)
        DB-->>Ledger: the ORIGINAL transaction, unchanged
        Note over Ledger: post() replays by key WITHOUT comparing parameters:<br/>an amended amount or order_id books NOTHING new
    end
    Ledger-->>Merchants: transaction (original on replay)
    API->>Merchants: deposit_balance(merchant_id) -- signed SUM over postings
    Merchants-->>API: balance
    opt order_id given -- M3c Task 4
        Merchants->>Close: end_a_refunded_merchant_order(order, by="settlement", actor="admin:{id}")
        Close->>DB: SUM(charge) and SUM(returned) on this order -- refund.settled_in_full
        alt fully settled AND status in paid/fulfilling/fulfilled
            Close->>DB: order.status = "failed" + OrderEvent(order.failed, by=settlement)
            Close->>DB: on_order_status_changed -> merchant webhook order.status_changed
            Note over Close,DB: what ends an order is that the money is back, not who decided it.<br/>It lives HERE and not in the button so the runbook's curl and M4's<br/>cabinet cannot bypass it. Not gated on replay: closing is idempotent
        else partial, or already closed, or delivered
            Close-->>Merchants: nothing -- money is still owed, or there is nothing left to close
        end
    end
    API-->>Admin: 201 {transaction_id, amount + order_id = the transaction's, balance}
    Note over Admin: on a mismatched replay the response's amount and order_id are the<br/>ORIGINAL's, so the UI can compare them with what was submitted and warn
    Note over DB: an attributed credit is a DEBIT leg on merchant_deposit referencing the order,<br/>which is exactly what refunded_usd on the merchant's order read sums
